From: Matthew Bodenham <matthew@bodenham.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:44:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] =?UTF-8?q?x1600:=20M2=20device=20models=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20SFC+SPI-NAND,=20INTC,=20RTC,=20CGU;=20rootfs=20mounts?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Roots the boot at a mounted squashfs rootfs read from an emulated
SPI-NAND (VFS: Mounted root readonly on device 50:2), then into the
rcS module-load chain. Each model was pinned by a boot symptom
(trace-driven), per docs/M1-bringup-log M2 section.

- SFC (ingenic_sfc_v2) + SPI-NAND: CDT command engine (0x9f read id,
  0x0f/0x1f get/set feature, 0x13 page read, 0xd8 erase, 0x10 program
  exec) over a PIO FIFO (reg 0x1000) + DMA descriptor chains (reg 0x90).
  GD5F1GQ4UC chip (0xC8/0xD1). ROW_ADDR=0x84 / COL_ADDR=0x80. Backed by
  a raw page+OOB image (2112 B/page, 1024 blocks); OOB 0xFF (no bad
  blocks). The 0x90 descriptor base is a guest virtual address (kseg1
  alias) -> phys = 0x90 - 0x20000000.
- INTC: real jz4780-style controller (2x32 banks, IMR resets all-masked,
  IPR = ISR & ~IMR) with the output wired to CPU IRQ line 2 — delivers
  the SFC (line 7) and UART (line 51) interrupts the kernel now takes.
- RTC: write-protocol model (+0x00 bit7 write-ready, +0x3c 0xa55a key
  then bit31 write-accepted). The plain stub made every write time out
  and the set-time retry spun the CPU in a +0x3c read storm.
- CGU: persistent regfile + PLL-status (+0x2c) reads all-locked, so the
  clock framework's clk_set_rate lock poll (used by the MSC clock)
  completes instead of retrying forever.

Boot now: rootfs + devtmpfs mount, ~14 soc_* modules load (i2c/aic
oops on unmapped 0x10050000/0x10079000 are non-fatal), then parks in
the soc_msc (SD card) probe before any MSC MMIO — the MSC no-card path
is the next model.
